{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5398-1","published":"2026-11-20T16:05:48Z","modified":"2026-11-21T10:00:05.323348997Z","related":["CVE-2026-115560","CVE-2026-126714","CVE-2026-127960","CVE-2026-128064","CVE-2026-128090","CVE-2026-129289","CVE-2026-129291","CVE-2026-129292","CVE-2026-129481","CVE-2026-129496","CVE-2026-129506","CVE-2026-129538","CVE-2026-15353"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-115560","CVE-2026-126714","CVE-2026-127960","CVE-2026-128064","CVE-2026-128090","CVE-2026-129289","CVE-2026-129291","CVE-2026-129292","CVE-2026-129481","CVE-2026-129496","CVE-2026-129506","CVE-2026-129538","CVE-2026-15353"],"summary":"Security update for php8","details":"This update for php8 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-15353: SOAP information disclosure through malformed array dimensions (bsc#1290681).\n- CVE-2026-115560: possible RCE via session upload `progress()` (bsc#1289303).\n- CVE-2026-126714: partially overwritten session files can lead to remote code execution (bsc#1290690).\n- CVE-2026-127960: denial of service through folded HTTP response headers (bsc#1290689).\n- CVE-2026-128064: mixed-case HTTPS and FTPS URLs can expose data in plaintext (bsc#1290688).\n- CVE-2026-128090: PHAR OpenSSL signature bypass via algorithm downgrade (bsc#1290684).\n- CVE-2026-129289: PHP-FPM request smuggling through an unread HTTP request body (bsc#1290687).\n- CVE-2026-129291: PHP-FPM epoll use-after-free can lead to local privilege escalation (bsc#1290692).\n- CVE-2026-129292: PHP-FPM status endpoint XSS via unescaped user and script fields (bsc#1290685).\n- CVE-2026-129496: timezone cache use-after-free can lead to remote code execution (bsc#1290686).\n- CVE-2026-129506: SOAP use-after-free when processing DTD entity references (bsc#1290683).\n- CVE-2026-129538: PHP-CGI out-of-bounds read and write during `PATH_INFO` correction (bsc#1290682).\n\nChanges for php8:\n\n- Version update to 8.3.37.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"apache2-mod_php8","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux